enforcement: |
  The reinvest rule is now checked, not just stated. tools/check-drift.sh check
  (i) compares every submodule copy of schema_lint.py (and unwrap-prose.py)
  against the hub's, so a fork can no longer diverge unnoticed. It found two on
  the day it shipped.
notes: |
  2026-08-23 schema-check.yml floats actions/checkout to @v7. This is the same
  bug the prose kit hit at 0.2.0 and agent-context at 0.3.1, missed here both
  times: the hub's own workflows moved to @v7 while this template stayed on
  @v4, so re-running the schema fan-out would have seeded a three-major
  DOWNGRADE into every adopting repo. Not a re-vendor — schema_lint.py,
  SCHEMA.template.md and CLAUDE.snippet.md are untouched, so the b2ffca1 parity
  contract below still holds
  (upstream's schema-check.yml is not part of the vendored payload; the fleet
  copy is already locally adapted via __DEFAULT_BRANCH__). No archive/ shape is
  needed: seed-schema.sh is additive-only (it skips a target that already has
  the workflow) and this kit has no --upgrade path, so nothing byte-compares
  against the outgoing text. The class is now gated — tools/check-drift.sh
  check (j) fails any seed template whose action major trails the hub's.

  2026-08-18 re-vendor (ce09aeb → b2ffca1):
  - Picks up everything the 2026-08-09 audit was waiting on: the SCHEMA#4
    self-registration fix (a schema registering its own SCHEMA.md row was
    reported as missing that file) and the federation layer — walks stop at
    git repo boundaries, `check --federation` verifies .gitmodules seams,
    `init` never scaffolds across a boundary. Directly relevant to this
    monorepo: the vendored linter now treats every projects/* mount as a
    foreign pyramid even without a terminal row.
  - tools/schema_lint.py stays byte-identical to upstream HEAD (the check (i)
    parity contract). Adopted submodules hold the older copy until re-seeded,
    so check (i) will warn on them — expected mid-upgrade state, resolve by
    re-running the schema fan-out per repo.
  - CLAUDE.snippet.md ports upstream's new submodule-mounts sentence into the
    fleet's one-paragraph-per-line reflow; the reflow remains deliberate local
    adaptation, not drift. SCHEMA.template.md is content-identical to upstream
    (quote/spacing style only).
  - Known gap (unchanged): the vendored copy has no local test coverage;
    upstream's suite (69 lint + 6 bench tests, green at b2ffca1) is the only
    verification beyond the hub's own pyramid linting clean.
